From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] libretro: expose the "Copy to texture" GPU readback mode

PPSSPP has three Skip GPU Readback modes (no skip, skip, copy to texture),
but the libretro core only maps its option to the first two: any value
other than "disabled" becomes SKIP. A game that reads a rendered
framebuffer back for effects (the Persona 4 port uses it for motion blur)
loses previous-frame data with SKIP, while NO_SKIP pays for a blocking
GPU-to-CPU readback on every transfer, which is very slow on Panfrost.
COPY_TO_TEXTURE keeps the copy on the GPU (CreateRAMFramebuffer plus
BlitFramebuffer) and is much faster.

Expose it as a third "texture" value of ppsspp_skip_gpu_readbacks. The
existing "disabled"/"enabled" values and the upstream default are kept, so
current configs and the nuubOS default (enabled) are unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/libretro/libretro_core_options.h
+++ b/libretro/libretro_core_options.h
@@ -18,6 +18,14 @@
    { NULL, NULL },       \
 }
 
+#define SKIP_GPU_READBACK_OPTIONS   \
+{                                   \
+   { "disabled", NULL },            \
+   { "enabled",  NULL },            \
+   { "texture",  NULL },            \
+   { NULL, NULL },                  \
+}
+
 #define MAC_ADDRESS_OPTIONS \
 {                           \
    { "0", NULL },           \
@@ -534,7 +542,7 @@
       "Some games require GPU readbacks, so be careful.",
       NULL,
       "hacks",
-      BOOL_OPTIONS,
+      SKIP_GPU_READBACK_OPTIONS,
       "disabled"
    },
    {
--- a/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -794,6 +794,8 @@
    {
       if (!strcmp(var.value, "disabled"))
          g_Config.iSkipGPUReadbackMode = (int)SkipGPUReadbackMode::NO_SKIP;
+      else if (!strcmp(var.value, "texture"))
+         g_Config.iSkipGPUReadbackMode = (int)SkipGPUReadbackMode::COPY_TO_TEXTURE;
       else
          g_Config.iSkipGPUReadbackMode = (int)SkipGPUReadbackMode::SKIP;
    }
